 ],
 "drivingQuestion": "Whose view does R' Elazar's ruling follow, and is it the halakha?",
 "outcome": "resolved",
 "outcomeNote": "R' Elazar is shown to follow R' Akiva; halakha rules like him.",
 "continuesQuestionOf": null,
 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "ketubot.40a.5",
   "daf": "40a",
   "sentenceId": 4,
   "he": "גְּמָ׳ אָמַר רַבָּה בַּר בַּר חָנָה אָמַר רַבִּי יוֹחָנָן: רַבִּי אֶלְעָזָר בְּשִׁיטַת רַבִּי עֲקִיבָא רַבּוֹ אֲמָרָהּ, דְּאָמַר: יֵשׁ לָהּ קְנָס וּקְנָסָהּ לְעַצְמָהּ. מִמַּאי — מִדְּקָתָנֵי: יְתוֹמָה, רַבִּי אֶלְעָזָר אוֹמֵר: הָאוֹנֵס חַיָּיב, וְהַמְפַתֶּה פָּטוּר.",
   "en": "«GEMARA:» «Rabba bar bar Ḥana said» that «Rabbi Yoḥanan said: Rabbi Elazar stated» his opinion «in accordance» with the opinion of «Rabbi Akiva, his teacher, as» with regard to a young woman who was betrothed and divorced and then raped, Rabbi Akiva «said» in an earlier mishna: «She is entitled to» a «fine» for rape «and her fine» is paid «to her.» Rabbi Yosei HaGelili says: She is not entitled to a fine for rape. «And from where» do we know that Rabbi Elazar’s opinion corresponds to the opinion of his teacher? «From» the fact «that» the mishna «teaches» with regard to «an orphan» that «Rabbi Elazar says: One who rapes» her «is obligated» to pay the fine «and one who seduces» her «is exempt» from payment."
  },
  {
   "id": "ketubot.40a.6",
   "daf": "40a",
   "sentenceId": 5,
   "he": "יְתוֹמָה, פְּשִׁיטָא? אֶלָּא הָא קָא מַשְׁמַע לַן דְּנַעֲרָה שֶׁנִּתְאָרְסָה וְנִתְגָּרְשָׁה, כִּיתוֹמָה. מָה יְתוֹמָה — לְעַצְמָהּ, אַף נַעֲרָה שֶׁנִּתְאָרְסָה וְנִתְגָּרְשָׁה — לְעַצְמָהּ.",
   "en": "The Gemara asks: «An orphan?» That is «obvious,» as she has no father and is not subject to the authority of anyone else. Clearly the seducer is exempt from payment because she was complicit. «Rather, this» is what the mishna is «teaching us: That» the legal status of «a young woman who was betrothed and divorced,» even if her father is alive, is «like» that of «an orphan: Just as» with regard to «an orphan,» payment of the fine is «to her, so too,» with regard to «a young woman who was betrothed and divorced,» payment of the fine is «to her.»"
  },
  {
   "id": "ketubot.40a.7",
   "daf": "40a",
   "sentenceId": 6,
   "he": "אָמַר רַבִּי זֵירָא אָמַר רַבָּה בַּר שֵׁילָא אָמַר רַב הַמְנוּנָא סָבָא אָמַר רַב אַדָּא בַּר אַהֲבָה אָמַר רַב: הֲלָכָה כְּרַבִּי אֶלְעָזָר. קָרֵי רַב עֲלֵיהּ דְּרַבִּי אֶלְעָזָר: ״טוּבְיָנָא דְחַכִּימֵי״.",
   "en": "«Rabbi Zeira said» that «Rabba bar Sheila said» that «Rav Hamnuna the Elder said» that «Rav Adda bar Ahava said» that «Rav said: The halakha is in accordance with» the opinion of «Rabbi Elazar. Rav» would «exclaim about Rabbi Elazar:» He is the «happiest of the Sages,» as he held that the halakha was ruled in accordance with his opinion in many instances."
  }
 ],
